---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Working-group meetings and records"
  description="How members prepare for meetings, contribute asynchronously and keep useful, consented records."
>
  <PageMeta category="Working groups · Member guide" variant="brand" updated="Meeting guidance · 21 August 2026" />
  <h1>Meetings and records</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Meetings concentrate discussion; they do not replace the persistent working record.
    Members should be able to prepare beforehand, contribute without attending live and
    inspect what happened afterwards.
  </p>

  <h2 id="before">Before a meeting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the agenda, candidate version, questions and evidence references named in the notice.</li>
    <li>Add a Teams reply or website comment early when clarification would help everyone prepare.</li>
    <li>Declare relevant affiliation, conflicts or material interests.</li>
    <li>Do not circulate a private meeting link or invitation beyond the approved group.</li>
    <li>Tell the organiser about accessibility needs or if asynchronous participation is required.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="during">What meetings should focus on</h2>
  <p>
    Useful meeting time is spent on scope, evidence, contested meaning, examples,
    counterexamples, open questions and review of visible candidate changes. Formal
    modelling can happen between meetings; participants are not expected to edit RDF,
    OWL, SKOS or SHACL in the session.
  </p>

  <h2 id="recording">Recording and transcription</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Recording or transcription must be announced and follow the agreed consent, access and retention conditions.</li>
    <li>A transcript should record its date, context and speakers where known.</li>
    <li>Sensitive or restricted discussion must not be copied into a public review surface.</li>
    <li>Audio and video files are not accepted as source-intake submissions; provide an authorised transcript instead.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="after">After a meeting</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Publish or circulate the permitted notes, transcript and action record.</li>
    <li>Link each substantive point to the relevant persistent question or review thread.</li>
    <li>State whether a point is evidence, a proposal, an unresolved issue or an agreed action.</li>
    <li>Give people who could not attend a clear asynchronous route and deadline for feedback.</li>
    <li>Carry only reviewed and recorded outcomes into the next candidate.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="authority">Meeting attendance is not authority</h2>
  <p>
    Attendance, silence, reactions and message volume do not by themselves establish
    consensus. ADR-0068 proposes a canonical issue record, asynchronous confirmation,
    consensus calls and ratification stages, but ADR-0068 remains proposed. Until OPDA
    adopts that lifecycle, pages must not present its exact thresholds or time windows as
    operative rules.
  </p>
  <p>
    The safe working principle is narrower: a decision discussed live should be posted
    with its rationale and affected candidate so absent members can inspect it, and no
    meeting-only statement should silently change the model.
  </p>
</Layout>
